      "content": "Even with \"borderline\" thyroid levels, any changes to your medication regimen without professional advice can be risky. Adderall, being a potent stimulant, can interact with your body's management of adrenal and thyroid hormones. Unintended consequences can range from exacerbating your current symptoms to causing new ones, or even affecting your heart rate or blood pressure. It's critical to adhere to the prescribed dosage until a healthcare professional evaluates your situation. Self-adjusting your medication increases the risk without a clear understanding of all potential interactions. Continue to seek your doctor's advice at the earliest opportunity. In the meantime, consider non-stimulative strategies to manage your work pressure and communicate your urgent need for medical attention.",
